// A color attribute names the part it colors.
//
// There used to be one ink word, `stroke:`, and it meant a different part on
// every kind — the border of a box, the text of a note or a glyph body, the
// line of a link. Coherent kind by kind, and it left exactly one thing with no
// way to say it: the color of the text on an ordinary box.
//
// `border:`, `text:` and `line:` name parts instead, so each means one thing
// everywhere and a word is refused on a kind that has no such part.

diagram background: #111111

// A box has three inkable parts and now a word for each of them.
box ledger "Ledger / append only"  fill: #142814  border: #486544  text: #cfe8c4  subtext: muted

// The part that could not be said before: text alone, on the default box.
box plain "Plain"  right of ledger (gap: wide)  text: #ff9d4d

// A note is bare text, so `text:` is the only color it takes. `border:` here
// is an error rather than a no-op, which is the point of naming parts.
note remark "a note is text and nothing else"  below ledger  text: #66ccff

// A style shared between boxes and links writes one key per kind. A style
// contributes a part only to the kinds that have it, so the box takes the
// border and the link takes the line, and neither sees the other's word.
style traced  border: #d2904e  line: #d2904e

// A glyph body is a picture and the text under it. Same one part.
box store "store"  right of plain (gap: wide)  shape: database  text: #ff9d4d

// On a link the line and the label are separate parts. The label still takes
// the line's color when it says nothing, so an orange link says orange in its
// words too — `text:` is how that is overridden.
box worker "Worker"  below remark (gap: wide)  style: traced
box queue  "Queue"   right of worker (gap: wide)  level with worker
link worker -> queue  "inherits the line"  style: traced  from: right  to: left

box reader "Reader"  below worker (gap: wide)
box cache  "Cache"   right of reader (gap: wide)  level with reader
link reader -> cache  "says its own"  line: #ff9d4d  text: #d9d9d9  from: right  to: left
